WEBVTT

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:08.810
1st Place - Len Tsukimori
2nd Place - Azuma Yunoki
3rd Place - Keiichi Shimizu
4th Place - Shoko Fuyuumi
5th Place - Kazuki Hihara
6th Place - Kahoko Hino

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:08.810
Maintenance?

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:10.200
Yup.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.020
The magic that was cast on the violin doesn't last forever.

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:17.960
So it needs magic recast on it in order to keep it in top shape.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:19.290
Here goes!

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:26.970
All right, it should be fine now.

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:28.760
That's it?

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:32.800
Yeah. Also, looks like you've practicing quite a bit.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.050
You gave a great performance yesterday.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.020
But I finished in last place.

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:43.730
That's because of the issues that happened before you even started performing, like your appearance.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:45.200
Also, your accompaniment.

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:47.140
I see...

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:52.760
But I'm really happy! You really worked hard for me!

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:53.780
Lili...

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:55.180
And also...

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:57.740
Lili?

00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:01.580
All that ruckus yesterday made me think of something good.

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:02.790
Huh?

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:05.170
Uhh, ladies and gentlemen,

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:09.870
we will be having a late entry into the music competition.

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:11.380
It couldn't be...

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:14.730
General Studies, class 2-5, Ryotaro Tsuchiura-kun.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.700
General Studies, class 2-5, Ryotaro Tsuchiura, will be joining from the 2nd selection.

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:16.640
What he said!

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.080
You're too much!

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:57.150
The Uneasy Polka

00:02:57.950 --> 00:02:59.280
I'm taking off!

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:03.240
Today, all the participants in the competition are going to music camp.

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:06.130
I'm not gonna make it in time!

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:11.120
Azuma-sama, how many days will you be going this time?

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:13.130
Three nights and four days.

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:16.120
I see. Have a good time.

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:18.980
Sure. Thank you.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:22.630
A good time, huh?

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:32.170
Man, what a waste of a long weekend.

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:35.890
You're telling me. Why send us to music camp all of a sudden?

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:37.070
Hey!

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:39.920
Kanayan! Tsuchiura!

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:42.570
I made it here on time!

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:46.410
I was so psyched, I couldn't sleep all night!

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:48.830
And then I overslept and man, was it a mess!

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.600
Where're the others?

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.600
Hey, make that kid shut up.

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:52.270
He's still my sempai, unfortunately.

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:57.440
You don't need to be so nervous, Hino-san.

00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:58.730
O-OK.

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:03.400
Come to think of it, I haven't had the chance to get to know you.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.110
How long have you been playing violin?

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:08.810
I'm actually a complete beginner.

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:14.780
Oh no! He's gonna think I'm a weirdo by saying I'm a beginner!

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:17.200
I actually heard a rumor about that.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:19.150
U-Umm...

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:24.600
I guess I should just say that it's my first year playing, or something.

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:27.320
I'm always so arrogant.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:34.370
It's this sort of attitude that caused Shoji-san to do what she did.

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:37.260
So I can't say that I'm just a beginner,

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:41.840
or that I'm being forced to compete anymore, huh?

00:05:31.670 --> 00:05:33.470
Holy cow...

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:34.840
This is...

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:38.410
Actually, we were allowed use of Fuyuumi-san's family villa.

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:40.440
Fuyuumi-san's villa?!

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:43.970
You can leave your bags here and we'll get started on dinner-

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:50.530
This is... How can I put it...

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:52.370
A blend of Japanese and Western decorations?

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:56.690
I'm sorry. My father likes it this way.

00:05:56.690 --> 00:05:58.920
But the practice rooms are normal.

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:01.420
What?! You have practice rooms?!

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:05.520
Of course. That's why we borrowed it.

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:07.750
There are three soundproof practice rooms.

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:10.600
They all house both an upright and a grand piano.

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:13.090
That really is incredible...

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:15.320
Chow time!

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:24.290
Hihara, calm down when you eat!

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:27.300
That's rude to Tomida-san who made all this food!

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:29.120
Oh, it's quite all right.

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:30.930
Oh, right.

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:35.110
It's always a mad scramble for food with my older brothers at home...

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:36.430
A mad scramble?

00:06:36.430 --> 00:06:40.740
I think I understand. My younger brother also eats quite a bit.

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:41.830
Oh?

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:46.010
Anyway, regarding the second selection's theme.

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:49.300
Sensei, you said you wouldn't tell us unless we came here.

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:54.700
Oh, Tsukimori-kun... We're just having a good time eating dinner.

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:58.210
I didn't come here to have a good time eating dinner.

00:06:58.210 --> 00:07:02.060
Right, right. Look forward to it on the last day.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:03.780
Kanazawa-sensei...

00:07:05.010 --> 00:07:08.460
I was supposed to have Oke club practice tomorrow and the next day!

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:11.020
I have to call Osaki-sempai!

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:17.090
By "Oke club" he must mean an orchestra, right?

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:19.280
Who is this sempai he mentioned?

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:22.680
Oh, Osaki is an alumnus.

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:26.070
Seems he likes helping out the Orchestra club.

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:30.970
Also, he's a violinist who won the last competition.

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:34.590
He volunteers? What a great person!

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:36.150
Speaking of extracurricular activities,

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:39.970
Tsuchiura, are you OK balancing things with the soccer team?

00:07:41.590 --> 00:07:43.220
I'm still figuring it out.

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:45.800
Oh.

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:51.630
I think I just ate something really delicious,

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:54.160
but I was thinking about something at the time,

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:56.310
so I can't remember what it was.

00:07:57.220 --> 00:08:01.820
I guess I'll know if I try them all again.

00:08:01.820 --> 00:08:04.020
Huh?

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:07.210
Tsuchiura-kun!

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:09.460
Huh? What is it, Hino?

00:08:09.700 --> 00:08:11.710
Umm,

00:08:11.710 --> 00:08:15.500
I was wondering if you're really going to be OK with the soccer team.

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:21.200
I mean, I'm the one who dragged you into this competition.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:24.850
What? You're the one who wanted me to play the piano.

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:26.010
That's true, but...

00:08:26.430 --> 00:08:29.970
Anyway, I haven't decided if I'm going to participate or not yet.

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:31.030
Huh?

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:33.950
Just kidding.

00:08:34.170 --> 00:08:37.580
Don't worry about it. It's not your fault.

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:40.950
See ya.

00:08:42.690 --> 00:08:44.990
Don't worry about it, huh?

00:08:44.990 --> 00:08:46.910
You say that, but...

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:49.930
I can't help being worried!

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:57.230
Hino-sempai, please use the bed. I brought a futon.

00:08:57.230 --> 00:08:58.130
Huh?

00:08:58.130 --> 00:09:03.230
It's fine. The bed is rather large, so I don't mind sharing it with you.

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:04.390
Huh?

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:09.000
Oh, no! If you're not OK with that, let's sleep separately, Fuyuumi-chan.

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:11.350
No, it's not that.

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:15.090
"Fuyuumi-chan"?

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:19.140
Oh, I thought it'd be easier if I called you that.

00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:20.990
I guess that was too forward of me.

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:22.260
No.

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:24.760
I'm happy.

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:30.960
What's with the racing heart?

00:09:35.930 --> 00:09:38.350
Oh, you're still awake.

00:09:38.350 --> 00:09:40.100
You got a problem with it?

00:09:40.340 --> 00:09:43.300
I can't believe I have to share a room with you.

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:45.830
My sentiments exactly.

00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:48.540
So yeah, you're on the soccer team, huh?

00:09:49.090 --> 00:09:51.500
How are you going to balance that with the competition?

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:53.880
That's none of your business.

00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:55.980
That's irrelevant.

00:09:57.070 --> 00:10:02.520
If you're not going to give 100% to the competition, you're just a nuisance.

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:03.830
I get it.

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:05.130
Because you're in the Music Department,

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:09.760
you mean to say we have different priorities when it comes to music?

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:12.040
So?

00:10:12.700 --> 00:10:15.540
Look, Hino-san finished dead last.

00:10:15.540 --> 00:10:18.700
Doesn't that say everything about you guys?

00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:20.630
What did you say?!

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:37.220
The competition, huh?

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:39.950
You just helped me make up my mind.

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:43.650
Thank you, Tsukimori.

00:12:06.430 --> 00:12:10.450
Good morning, Tsukimori-kun, Tsuchiura-kun.

00:12:11.820 --> 00:12:13.410
Please change our room!

00:12:11.820 --> 00:12:13.410
Please change our room!

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:16.420
Huh?

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:26.200
Huh, Tsuchiura?

00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:29.640
You're playing in here!

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:33.060
And, aren't you enjoying it a little too much?

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:34.630
A-All the other pianos are taken!

00:12:34.630 --> 00:12:37.430
Sorry for interrupting your practice.

00:12:37.430 --> 00:12:40.230
I heard all the CDs are in here.

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:41.780
CDs?

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:43.730
Oh, those.

00:12:43.730 --> 00:12:45.790
I'm just taking a break.

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:48.280
I'm looking for a music grammar chart.

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:54.960
So, are Yunoki-sempai, Tsukimori, and Fuyuumi using the practice rooms?

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:57.950
I-I-I'm sorry.

00:12:57.950 --> 00:13:00.980
Hey, did you do something, Tsuchiura-kun?

00:13:00.980 --> 00:13:02.560
N-No!

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:06.330
Anyway, Hino-chan, what sort of CDs are you looking for?

00:13:06.330 --> 00:13:09.260
I was hoping there'd be something easy to practice.

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:12.020
Then you'll want a collection of short pieces.

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:13.140
Short pieces?

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:19.700
Short pieces are free compositions that are only a few minutes long.

00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:22.530
If it's for the violin, Kreisler is famous.

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:25.140
I see. Kreisler, huh?

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:27.880
Speaking of Kreisler...

00:13:27.880 --> 00:13:29.330
He was a liar.

00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:33.800
A liar?

00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:41.510
He would release his own compositions, but said they were made by famous composers of the past.

00:13:41.510 --> 00:13:48.940
Well, there weren't any soft-minded critics who'd acknowledge unknown musicians back then.

00:13:48.940 --> 00:13:51.960
So he'd use the names of famous composers?

00:13:52.910 --> 00:13:54.490
That's...

00:13:54.490 --> 00:13:58.930
That's a magic violin. Anyone can play it.

00:13:58.930 --> 00:14:04.610
But since his compositions are well regarded nowadays,

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:08.360
it must have been a rather effective lie.

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:09.120
Huh?

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:12.650
He must have been a likable man.

00:14:12.650 --> 00:14:16.330
He liked to pull pranks on people, but he was an honest, kind man.

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:24.060
Among violinists, he truly set out to instill to make people enjoy music.

00:14:24.060 --> 00:14:26.030
Enjoy music?

00:14:26.030 --> 00:14:30.130
Don't the characters for "music" in your language, Japanese, mean "to enjoy sound"?

00:14:30.130 --> 00:14:33.510
Kreisler is sort of like Lili.

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:36.520
A lying violinist, huh?

00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:40.140
But his music was the real thing.

00:14:40.140 --> 00:14:43.220
That's why, even today, many people are drawn to it.

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:50.400
I wonder if I'll be able to play by own my own skill someday, and not just through magic.

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:23.800
I'll give it my all!

00:15:28.270 --> 00:15:29.870
What's the matter, Hino-chan?

00:15:29.870 --> 00:15:34.450
I-I practiced for so many hours that my body aches...

00:15:34.450 --> 00:15:37.020
Really? You all right?

00:15:37.020 --> 00:15:41.730
Do you exercise, Hihara-sempai?

00:15:41.730 --> 00:15:44.830
I used to go running every day.

00:15:45.450 --> 00:15:48.720
Because of that, I've got great lung capacity now.

00:15:50.390 --> 00:15:53.780
That smile really suits Hihara-sempai.

00:15:53.780 --> 00:15:56.410
OK, this is for you.

00:15:56.410 --> 00:15:57.400
Huh?

00:15:58.840 --> 00:16:00.590
This is pure bliss!

00:16:00.590 --> 00:16:03.310
You really eat a lot, don't you?

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:05.380
There's always room for sweets!

00:16:05.380 --> 00:16:07.810
Still, this is too much.

00:16:07.810 --> 00:16:13.110
Oh, right, you ended up switching rooms after all, huh?

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:13.860
Yeah.

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:15.420
Oh yeah, Tsuchiura,

00:16:15.420 --> 00:16:17.950
will you talk to Shimizu-kun about the bed situation?

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:22.060
Oh, I'm fine with the sofa.

00:16:22.060 --> 00:16:25.480
It's fine. I had my eyes set on the sofa anyway.

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:26.930
You don't need to be so considerate.

00:16:26.930 --> 00:16:29.400
No, I'm not, really...

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:32.120
It's fine. Use the bed!

00:16:32.120 --> 00:16:33.620
No, you should!

00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:35.230
Don't worry about it!

00:16:35.230 --> 00:16:36.220
No, you don't worry about it!

00:16:36.220 --> 00:16:37.530
I'm fine!

00:16:37.530 --> 00:16:38.670
Me too!

00:16:38.670 --> 00:16:40.370
The bed should go to the sempai.

00:16:40.370 --> 00:16:42.390
No, since I'm your sempai, it should go to you!

00:16:44.130 --> 00:16:45.870
St-Stop that, you two!

00:16:49.760 --> 00:16:50.980
Hihara-sempai!

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:13.090
How long were you gonna stay on top of her?

00:17:18.060 --> 00:17:21.110
S-S-Sorry, Hino-chan!

00:17:21.610 --> 00:17:24.720
No, I pulled you down with me.

00:17:24.720 --> 00:17:28.200
Umm, err, uh...

00:17:28.200 --> 00:17:30.450
I should call it a night.

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:36.070
Hino-chan...

00:17:49.640 --> 00:17:51.220
Hey!

00:17:55.640 --> 00:17:58.590
Something the matter, Tsukimori-kun?

00:17:58.590 --> 00:17:59.600
No.

00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:02.110
That was Hino-san just now, right?

00:18:02.520 --> 00:18:04.880
She's really working hard.

00:18:04.880 --> 00:18:09.590
It's really incredible to think she only just started playing the violin.

00:18:10.090 --> 00:18:14.070
Impossible. The violin takes years to play.

00:18:14.340 --> 00:18:19.240
But she said herself that she's only been playing a little while.

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:23.430
Supposedly she didn't even pick up a violin until she entered the competition.

00:18:23.430 --> 00:18:27.710
When I heard that, I was shocked myself.

00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:31.250
For a girl like that to exist, she must be...

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:32.910
A virtuoso.

00:18:45.230 --> 00:18:48.010
He got so close to me all of a sudden.

00:18:48.410 --> 00:18:50.980
So close, I could feel his breath.

00:18:50.980 --> 00:18:54.150
Wait, why am I thinking about this?!

00:18:55.310 --> 00:18:59.070
I guess he is a boy.

00:19:02.850 --> 00:19:07.050
How could I have done that to a girl?!

00:19:07.460 --> 00:19:11.200
It's fine. You didn't do it on purpose.

00:19:11.200 --> 00:19:14.640
Yeah. But I'm gonna apologize properly tomorrow.

00:19:14.640 --> 00:19:16.450
That'd be for the best.

00:19:16.450 --> 00:19:18.520
Also...

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:24.670
Girls are so soft... and smell sorta nice, huh?

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:27.520
S-Sempai!

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:31.480
No! I mean, they're different from guys...

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:33.050
Of course they are.

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:38.540
Wait, Tsuchiura... Have you dated a girl before?

00:19:38.540 --> 00:19:40.020
Oh, no...

00:19:40.840 --> 00:19:43.240
Super Intrigued

00:19:41.750 --> 00:19:43.260
What's it like?

00:19:44.060 --> 00:19:46.030
It's no big deal.

00:19:46.030 --> 00:19:50.070
So you did lie to me! Are you dating one now?!

00:19:50.070 --> 00:19:51.910
I told you, I'm-

00:19:51.910 --> 00:19:53.360
Is it Hino-chan?!

00:19:54.810 --> 00:19:58.230
N-Not really. We're not like that.

00:19:58.230 --> 00:20:01.230
Oh, that's great.

00:20:03.650 --> 00:20:05.300
"That's great"?

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:11.970
Wh-Why did I say that's great?

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:16.210
I get it, Hihara-sempai.

00:20:16.210 --> 00:20:17.450
Let's call it a night.

00:20:17.450 --> 00:20:19.360
Come on. Go to bed.

00:20:19.360 --> 00:20:21.320
Y-Yeah.

00:20:24.940 --> 00:20:28.070
What am I all flustered about?

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:42.840
Hino-chan?

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:48.920
Hihara-sempai.

00:20:48.920 --> 00:20:50.200
I'm sorry about yesterday!

00:20:50.200 --> 00:20:51.020
Huh?

00:20:52.110 --> 00:20:55.600
D-Don't apologize to me, Hihara-sempai!

00:20:55.600 --> 00:20:59.120
It's my fault for butting in, really. And I didn't clean up.

00:20:59.120 --> 00:21:02.230
No. I left you with such a bad memory.

00:21:02.230 --> 00:21:03.340
No, I...

00:21:03.620 --> 00:21:04.800
No, I...

00:21:08.260 --> 00:21:10.030
This is strange.

00:21:10.030 --> 00:21:11.220
Yeah.

00:21:11.220 --> 00:21:15.680
But I did want to apologize to you, so...

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:17.880
Hihara-sempai...

00:21:18.970 --> 00:21:21.250
This is embarrassing.

00:21:21.250 --> 00:21:23.510
Are you practicing in the garden again today, Hino-chan?

00:21:23.510 --> 00:21:24.580
Oh, yes.

00:21:24.580 --> 00:21:27.250
The breeze feels really nice outside.

00:21:27.250 --> 00:21:32.350
Yeah. But unlike yesterday, practice moderately.

00:21:32.350 --> 00:21:33.560
See ya!

00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:38.230
Hihara-sempai's cheerfulness really cheers me up.

00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:40.290
Moderately, huh?

00:21:40.290 --> 00:21:42.570
You must have a lot of free time.

00:21:42.570 --> 00:21:43.850
Tsukimori-kun.

00:21:46.470 --> 00:21:48.000
Is something wrong?

00:21:54.230 --> 00:21:57.540
Are you gonna pull off your second selection?

00:21:57.540 --> 00:21:58.640
Huh?

00:21:58.640 --> 00:22:01.390
Are you for real,

00:22:01.390 --> 00:22:03.240
or are you a fraud?

00:23:36.380 --> 00:23:39.770
Lili's One Point Classic!

00:23:36.580 --> 00:23:39.770
Lili's One Point Classic

00:23:39.770 --> 00:23:43.620
Kreisler was born in 1875 in Vienna.

00:23:43.620 --> 00:23:47.410
He was a world-renown violinist and composer!

00:23:47.410 --> 00:23:50.100
He had a gift for music ever since he was a child.

00:23:50.100 --> 00:23:53.790
They even say he was able to read sheet music before letters!

00:23:54.270 --> 00:23:56.250
OK, now time for a quiz.

00:23:56.250 --> 00:24:02.550
How old was Kreisler when he was admitted into the music academy in Vienna?

00:24:02.550 --> 00:24:05.110
The answer is at the end of this program!

00:24:05.110 --> 00:24:09.200
Next Episode

00:24:05.480 --> 00:24:09.870
With the moon shining so brightly in the night sky, it just makes me want to play the violin.

00:24:09.870 --> 00:24:11.170
This may be sudden, Hino-san,

00:24:11.170 --> 00:24:12.050
but when did you start playing the violin?

00:24:12.050 --> 00:24:15.550
U-Umm, I don't remember.

00:24:15.550 --> 00:24:17.890
Next episode: The Secret Duet.

00:24:17.890 --> 00:24:20.090
What? Just the two of us?!

00:24:20.500 --> 00:24:21.850
The answer is...

00:24:22.450 --> 00:24:25.100
Seven years old!
